; worldswitch.eval - what a world switch must not carry over, and when it must
; not happen (code-review C115, C234). Judged by tools/EditorTest.py phase 30,
; on two scratch worlds: et_demo (opened with -project) and et_other beside it.
;
; 1. A QUESTION DOES NOT CROSS (C115). The exit's question is asked (`confirm
;    leave` - what stepping onto an exit stair asks), then `worlds load
;    et_other`. The question names this world's dungeon and its Yes would run
;    LeaveDungeon; in the next world it must be gone, taken down by the UNLOAD
;    - its log line names which ending took it - before that world's new game
;    could: a switch to a world that fails to load reaches no new game. A Yes is
;    then refused, there being nothing up to answer.
; 2. NO SWITCH UNDER A BAKE (C234). Back in et_demo, the create dialog's "Use
;    installed" on a floor set nobody paints and with no worn meshes
;    (et_switch_bake) starts AssetBaker; `worlds load et_other` is refused while
;    it runs; `bake wait` lets it land, which it does in et_demo, the world that
;    asked for it. A type from an installed set records no import.
; 3. ...NOR UNDER AN IMPORT (C234's other half: the imports.cat record). The
;    create dialog's Import, Browse handed a folder EditorTest wrote (one small
;    albedo map; ET_IMPORT_DIR is replaced by its path), bakes in TWO runs - the
;    maps, then the worn meshes - and `worlds load et_other` is refused in each,
;    the second after the step 0 -> 1 hand-off. Both land in et_demo: the type in
;    floors.cat, the record in imports.cat. The script returns to et_demo first,
;    so this half is judged on its own whatever became of the second.
; EditorTest reads both worlds' manifests and catalogs off the disk: et_other's
; byte for byte as they were, imports.cat among them; et_demo's floors.cat
; gaining the two types and its imports.cat the one record, nothing else moved.

logecho on
reset
echo --- asked ---
confirm leave
confirm
echo --- switched ---
worlds load et_other
worlds status
confirm
expect-refuse confirm yes
echo --- back ---
worlds load et_demo
worlds status
; The editor open, as "+ New..." needs it.
editor
echo --- bake ---
newasset floors installed et_switch_bake et_switchbake
bake
expect-refuse worlds load et_other
worlds status
bake wait 300
echo --- landed ---
bake
newasset status
worlds status
echo --- import ---
worlds load et_demo
editor
newasset floors import ET_IMPORT_DIR et_switchimp
bake
expect-refuse worlds load et_other
worlds status
bake wait 300
echo --- import step 1 ---
bake
expect-refuse worlds load et_other
worlds status
bake wait 300
echo --- imported ---
bake
newasset status
worlds status
echo --- end ---
